{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (Phase 1 only; no fix landed): The five `test_atomic_completion_close.py` failures are host-harness environment contamination, not a missing `refs/heads/tickets` ref and not a Git 2.55 push/default-branch change. This session inherits `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=3` with `GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=safe.bareRepository` / `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=explicit`, which overrides the user's global `safe.bareRepository=all`. The failing assertions call the test helper `_git(remote, ...)` on a bare fixture remote (`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py:40-46`, remote created/pushed in `_ticket_remote` at :102-117), and Git refuses that read with `fatal: cannot use bare repository ... (safe.bareRepository is 'explicit')`. Inspection of the failed fixture remotes with `git -c safe.bareRepository=all -C <remote> rev-parse refs/heads/tickets` proves the ref exists. Discriminating experiment: running the same target file with only the injected `GIT_CONFIG_*` entries removed, still using host `git version 2.55.0`, passes: `17 passed in 40.47s`. A minimal Git 2.55 push to a bare remote likewise creates `refs/heads/tickets` when the injected config is absent. CI impact: expected none for Gerrit Verified; `_build-and-test.yml`/`gerrit-verify.yaml` run on `ubuntu-latest`, install Python 3.12/uv, and do not set this Copilot harness `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT` override. Disposition: accepted as environment/config; local full-suite pre-flight in this harness may show this cluster red unless `GIT_CONFIG_*` injection is sanitized or bare-remote test helpers opt in to safe bare access. No code fix landed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788474792198800271,"uuid":"15d974be-9f21-48d8-8ff2-9af68078948f"}